---
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/run-loop-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/run-loop-dark.svg?raw';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={460}
  caption="The loop that ran all night: one unit at a time, nothing merged without green checks and a recorded verdict, and a STOP that parks the work instead of improvising."
>
  The plan and pre-flight come first, with every decision made up front. The
  orchestrator writes one brief per unit. An executor works in its own git
  worktree and opens a pull request. CI runs on the final commit. A review
  follows: a hostile agent with fresh context for risky units, or the
  orchestrator's own read for the rest. REVISE sends it back to the
  executor, APPROVE lets it merge, and a merge is a production deploy. The orchestrator checks the live
  site, a row goes into the run ledger, and the next unit starts.
  If an executor hits a STOP condition, it writes a BLOCKED line and waits
  for me instead.
</Diagram>
